# Check out every file byte-for-byte as it is stored, on every platform.
#
# The release job runs on Linux and compares the files inside each packaged
# app.asar with the repository's own. Git for Windows otherwise rewrites text
# files with CRLF on checkout, so the Windows-built archive could never match
# and the release was refused ("app.asar content mismatch: LICENSE"). It also
# keeps shell scripts runnable: a CRLF shebang does not execute.
* -text
